Main Branch 1.0.85345 Release 2026-11-04

Headline changes

Stunned units are immune from being re-stunned
Added a Players Screen (F9) showing a consolidated view of all known nations
Performance optimization

Known Issues

Old World on Mac does not currently work correctly with the latest version of the GOG Galaxy launcher (version 2.1).  
A fix is planned for the next update, in the meantime please use the previous version of GOG Galaxy (version 2.0) 

Design

Stunned units are immune from being re-stunned
Increased Ruthless AI war declaration probability when the player is close to winning
Tribe camp clear events now only trigger once per camp, subsequent camp clears give resources instead
Tribe units with an alliance to another player are more expensive to hire and recruit
Religious conversion now happens immediately on founding a religion, to ensure that the initial religion head will belong to the founding player
Religion head priority is given to characters from a family with a city of that religion
Empires of the Indus DLC now enabled 50% of the time in Game of the Week, as for other DLCs
Default map scripts no longer allow the distance between city sites to go below the minimum (8)
Added No Mountains option to Wetlands map script (Empires of the Indus)
Reduced the size of Duel of the Ancient maps that don't have water outside or between the paths (Empires of the Indus)


Programming

Performance optimization
Improved pathfinder efficiency
Optimized game saving to XML
Units processed before characters again
Converted Stun cooldown to a unit effect
Changed Immobile to a unit effect instead of a cooldown


UI

Added a Players Screen (F9) showing a consolidated view of all known nations
Added new notifications about known rival player state changes: relative power, relative knowledge, increase in best city culture, when they get 1, 4, or 7 laws
Important character notifications are shown in the notification icon tooltips even if they are not included in the turn summary
CTRL+clicking a mission now allows cancelling an active character mission and starting the new one in one click
Notable (pinned or with notable trait or relationship) character updates are among those included in notifications
Cycle buttons are now only draggable with right click, to prevent accidental re-ordering
Added game list refresh button to the main menu
Reversed Cloud Games screen listing order
Added additional helptext for right-click & drag to reorder cycle buttons
Moved inactive bonuses to Potential Bonuses link on Connected and Citizen tooltips. Potential Bonuses are hidden when Advanced Help Text is not enabled
Removed some redundant terrain checks for Bath improvements
OS user name is no longer used as a fallback for player name when platform nickname not available
Tweaked display of turns remaining on applied unit effect tooltips
Appended tech card concept help to the tech tree status icon tooltip
Pending decisions can be skipped to end your turn early if there is an unpaused dynamic turn timer, or if the turn style is not strict


Bugs Fixed

Fixed AI giving non-military units (especially Settlers) lower priority than intended
Fixed worker kill opinion penalty not being applied
Fixed observer momentarily auto-switching to observe AI players
Fixed victory conditions sometimes being triggered by temporary effectPlayer changes
Fixed bug with event system seed consistency
Fixed server sometimes changing AI players to human on load
Fixed server mode not being properly set on load
Fixed switching observed players resetting the chat options
Fixed attempting to join a network game when join already in progress causing an error
Fixed pathfinder bugs
Fixed random event options not being truly random
Fixed AI development extra starting units not getting allocated a family
Fixed Ruthless AI war declaration probability increase not being applied
Fixed improvement ambitions not completing the turn of a leader's death
Fixed an AI assert
Fixed event granted critical chance modifier bonus not resetting after attack
Fixed free specialist border expansion not happening when tile is pillaged
Fixed load/save error
Fixed UU tech cards going directly in the draw pile when their culture requirement is satisfied
Fixed player email not being updated when not done from within an ongoing game
Fixed AI issue with not clearing cached current military unit number
Fixed bug in water control tile prediction for anchored tiles that are farther than the ship's water control range
Fixed network not being disconnected after multiple attempts with a full send queue
Fixed nested submenus closing when clicking on the text area of context buttons
Fixed family head not updating immediately when current head leaves the nation
Fixed Korean age helptext
Fixed German event text translation issues
Fixed scenarios showing The New for difficulty in Hall of Fame (will now show Custom)
Fixed extra Antigonid vision at the start of Heroes of the Aegean scenario 6
Fixed bug where hiring a player unit would increase as you hired more tribal units (affects mods only)
